      "content": "That makes a lot of sense for my paper. So, if we were actually presenting this to a jury, are you saying the prosecution's case would basically fall apart if they relied on Witness B? Like, would a jury naturally be more skeptical of a young Hispanic guy in a hoodie than a man in a suit, even if the facts they saw were the same? It feels like the physical appearance and the race are doing more work here than the actual testimony is.",
